---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
// Italics for the <em> on this page only: Geist Mono for the lead under the
// heading, Montserrat for the text. The rest of the site does not load them,
// and font-synthesis is off, so emphasis elsewhere stays upright.
import "@fontsource/geist-mono/500-italic.css";
import "@fontsource/montserrat/500-italic.css";
---
<BaseLayout title="About">
  <div class="container article-page">
    <div class="eyebrow">about</div>
    <h1>Hello, Cami</h1>
    <p class="article-lead"><em>Curious, open-minded and slightly hyperactive</em></p>

    <div class="prose about-prose">

      <p>
        This is more of an informal introduction to who I am than a professional introduction
      </p>

      <p>
        My name is Camily. I’m a computer scientist who graduated in 2025.
        I currently live in Curitiba, Brazil, although I’ve spent a good part of my
        life moving between different cities. I’ve lived in eight so far, which I 
        think made me pretty adaptable and gave me an early sense of how big the
        world actually is.
      </p>

      <p>
        I would define myself as a very curious person. I have a suspicious number of unfinished side projects 
        and a very limited ability to look at an interesting idea and think: 
        <em>"maybe I don’t need to do anything with this"</em>.
      </p>

       <p>
        My interests tend to wander a lot between philosophy, technology, art, psychology,
        current events, or some completely random idea I stumbled across at 1 a.m.
        Even when I decide not to deep dive into something, I still feel the need to
        write it down somewhere, just in case.
      </p>

      <p>
        I also tend to think in first principles. If I can understand the basic pieces
        of something, I feel like I can reason my way through the rest. There is a quote I really like:
      </p>

      <blockquote>
        If you know the first principles of something, you can build the rest of
        your knowledge around them to produce something new.
      </blockquote>

  
      <p>
        On the technical side, I have a particular weakness for DevOps,
        distributed systems, infrastructure, Machine Learning, Data Engineering and LLMs.
        I’m especially interested in understanding how these technologies
        work underneath the abstractions we usually interact with.
      </p>

      <p>
        Outside of tech, I like hackathons, video games, movies, music, books and
        whittling. Basically, it's just: 
        <em>"that looks interesting, I should try it"</em>.
      </p>

      <p>
        I played fingerstyle guitar for a few years. I’ve also tried painting,
        drawing, and writing short stories. More recently, I bought a Swiss Army
        knife because I decided I wanted to learn whittling and make small wooden
        sculptures. I have a funny story from my first few weeks of learning it... SPOILER!
        it ended with a big scar on the palm of my hand.
      </p>

      <p>
        I really enjoy working with other people and bouncing ideas around, 
        even though I can be a little reserved and shy at first.
        If you ever need someone for a hackathon team, I’m probably in.
        I’m also always up for talking about IT and ML. Feel free to reach out to me on LinkedIn.
      </p>

         
      
      <p>
        So yeah, that’s me. Sorry about the long intro btw
      </p>


    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
